#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""issue-agent-review-audit: read-only evidence collector and metrics calculator for the
haechibot review-quality audit (project skill .claude/skills/haechibot-review-audit).

Subcommands
  collect --since ISO --until ISO --out DIR [--repo OWNER/NAME ...]
          [--reviewer LOGIN] [--evidence-days H]
      Pull GitHub evidence for every PR that LOGIN reviewed in [since, until) and write
      the unit files below. Read-only: every call is a `gh api` REST GET or a GraphQL
      query; nothing is ever mutated. Prints one short count line to stdout.
      --since ISO          window start, inclusive (ISO-8601; `Z` or offset; a bare date
                           means 00:00Z)
      --until ISO          window end, exclusive
      --out DIR            new output directory, created 0700; refused if it exists
      --repo OWNER/NAME    repeatable; default: isac322/cc-lb isac322/flareway
                           isac322/krema isac322/kwin-mcp isac322/pillar-csi isac322/rkmon
      --reviewer LOGIN     bot reviewer login (default: haechibot[bot])
      --evidence-days H    evidence horizon (default 3): a candidate is kept only if its
                           event time <= anchor + H; the anchor is the attributed bot
                           review's submitted_at, or merged_at for post-merge commits
                           (which also bounds the post-merge scan). Use the same H for
                           both windows; dropped counts go to manifest "evidence".

  metrics --dir DIR [--labels-findings F] [--labels-misses F] [--labels-judge F]
          [--labels-matcher F] [--exclude-pr [OWNER/]REPO#N ...] [--format md|json]
      Join label files with the unit files in DIR (plus DIR/panel.json and
      DIR/coverage.jsonl when present) and print the METRIC_KEYS figures with Wilson 95%
      intervals (z=1.96), broken down by repo, size_bucket, verdict (body verdict),
      author_type (owner / implementer_bot / automation / external), file_type and
      defect_type. Label files default to DIR/labels-*.jsonl. labels-judge.jsonl feeds
      only judge_bias (judge vs labelerB on irr_sample items); labels-matcher.jsonl feeds
      only match_kappa.defect_first / .review_first (each matcher order vs final on
      match_sample rows). --exclude-pr drops a PR
      and its label rows (repeatable). Rows that fail validation are listed under "bad
      rows" and excluded; they never abort the run.

  compare --before M.json --after M.json [--format md|json]
      Two `metrics --format json` outputs -> after - before for the D13 primary endpoints:
      validity_precision, noise_rate and approve_with_important_miss.per_pr
      (Newcombe hybrid-score difference CI + two-sided Fisher exact), and
      important_escaped_per_pr (exact conditional binomial test of equal per-PR rates).
      Other top-level proportions get a descriptive Newcombe CI. Warns when the two
      evidence horizons differ.

  kappa --a F --b F [--rater-a R] [--rater-b R] [--field NAME ...] [--all-items]
        [--format md|json]
      Agreement between two label files per field (validity, severity, bot_match,
      is_defect, verdict, p2_blocking): Cohen kappa with a 95% CI, linear weighted kappa
      for severity (quadratic as an extra), raw agreement, PABAK, positive/negative and
      per-category specific agreement. p2_blocking uses only items both raters rated P2
      (unset counts as false). Only irr_sample items unless --all-items.

  panel-draw --dir DIR --seed S [--n 10]
      Seeded stratified draw of N PRs over repo x verdict strata (automation PRs
      excluded; proportional largest-remainder allocation). Writes DIR/panel.json
      {seed, n, strata, prs: [{pr_id, target_head_sha, target_rule, stratum}]}; refuses
      to overwrite. Target head (D8): latest bot-reviewed head before the first
      non-PR-author fix commit, else the first GREEN head, else the final reviewed head.

Output files (collect). Every *.jsonl line is one JSON object with a stable "id".
Files are 0600 inside 0700 directories.
  prs.jsonl         id "<owner>/<repo>#<n>": repo, number, title, author,
                    author_association, author_type, state, merged, merged_at, base_ref,
                    base_sha_at_merge, final_head_sha, merge_commit_sha, created_at,
                    changed_files, additions, deletions, size_bucket (S <50 changed lines,
                    M <400, L >=400 or >=20 files), bot_review_ids, human_reviewers, raw_dir
  reviews.jsonl     id "<pr-id>@review/<review_id>": every review on the PR (bot and
                    human): pr_id, review_id, reviewer, event and github_state (raw GitHub
                    state; superseded bot reviews become DISMISSED), verdict (first
                    "**Verdict: GREEN|BLOCKING|OPEN**" line mapped to APPROVED /
                    CHANGES_REQUESTED / COMMENTED; github_state when absent),
                    is_reply_container (empty-body bot review without root comments; only
                    carries thread replies; ignored by metrics), reviewed_head_sha,
                    submitted_at, body, is_bot, in_window, finding_ids,
                    superseded_by_head, head_is_final
  findings.jsonl    id "<review-unit-id>/f<k>": one per bot finding (root inline comment,
                    or body bullet whose first token is P0-P3, outside "Previous findings",
                    without an inline twin on the same path within [start-3, end+3]):
                    pr_id, review_id, review_event, review_verdict, reviewed_head_sha,
                    submitted_at, in_window, file_type, source (inline|body), severity, path,
                    line, start_line,
                    side, title, body, comment_id, thread_id, thread_resolved,
                    thread_outdated, replies, changed_in_vicinity_1, changed_in_vicinity_5,
                    file_changed_later, vicinity_method (commit-walk|compare-fallback|null),
                    signal_note, next_bot_review_id, next_bot_review_status
                    (Closed|Open|absent), next_bot_review_line, author_reply_kind
                    (none|ack|reject|question)
  candidates.jsonl  content-addressed ids (stable across re-collection):
                    <pr-id>/hunk/<commit12|cmp-<a12>-<b12>>/<path>@-a,b+c,d  post_review_hunk
                    <pr-id>/comment/<review|review_comment|issue_comment>/<id>  human_comment
                    <pr-id>/postmerge/<sha12>                                post_merge_commit
                    <pr-id>/xref/<owner>/<repo>#<n>                          cross_reference
                    Every candidate has anchor_at, event_at and evidence_deadline.
                    human_comment adds commenter_kind (human|implementer_bot),
                    blind_to_bot, head_at_comment and, for human root inline comments,
                    is_root_inline, changed_in_vicinity_1 and author_reply_kind.
                    post_review_hunk covers non-merge commits after a bot-reviewed head
                    and, for reviews on force-pushed heads, the compare diff (source
                    "compare").
  coverage.jsonl    id "<pr-id>": heads, bot_reviewed_heads, foreign_fix_commits,
                    unreviewed_prefix_heads (head before a non-PR-author commit that never
                    got a bot review), merged_head_reviewed, attention_comments,
                    attention_only (PR with only bot failure/stop comments), has_gap
  manifest.json     args, collector_version, generated_at, counts per file, evidence
                    (evidence_days, dropped_after_horizon, horizon_after_run_time), heads
                    (reviews_on_force_pushed_heads, reviews_on_vanished_heads),
                    truncation counts, api_errors, skipped PRs, notes
  raw/<owner>__<repo>/<n>/
                    pr.json files.json commits.json reviews.json review_comments.json
                    issue_comments.json threads.json timeline.json commit-<sha>.json
                    compare-<sha>.json post_merge_commits.json: the raw API JSON behind
                    the unit rows

Label files (metrics input; vocabularies are the VOCAB table at the top of this script)
  labels-findings.jsonl  {id, rater (labelerA|labelerB|final), irr_sample, validity,
                          adjudicated_severity, p2_blocking, noise_codes, value,
                          author_action, defect_type, file_type, dedup_key, notes}
                          INVALID and SEVERITY_INFLATED are derived, never labelled.
  labels-misses.jsonl    {id "<candidate-id>[.<k>]@<head12>" (panel "<pr-id>/p<k>@<head12>",
                          owner session "<pr-id>/os<k>@<head12>"), rater, irr_sample,
                          match_sample, channel, verdict, exposed_by_pr, is_defect,
                          present_at_reviewed_head, reviewed_head_sha, latest_present_head,
                          adjudicated_severity, p2_blocking, bot_match, matched_finding_id,
                          review_id, defect_type, file_type, repo_rule, dedup_key, sources}
                          One row per (defect, bot-reviewed head where present); rows of
                          one defect share dedup_key. A partial match may name review_id
                          instead of matched_finding_id.
  labels-judge.jsonl     {id, rater "judge", validity}; labels-matcher.jsonl {id, rater
                          "matcher-defect_first" | "matcher-review_first" (or order),
                          bot_match}; both orders may label the same id.
  A miss row with out_of_horizon: true (verdict null) is accepted but excluded from
  every figure (counted in coverage.miss_rows_out_of_horizon). A row with coverage_only:
  true (defect fixed before any bot review; heads may be null, id may lack @<head12>) is
  kept out of R_imp and every miss figure and counted in coverage_unreviewed_defects.
  Rows with rater "final" drive the figures; labelerA/labelerB rows feed irr.

Assumptions and heuristics (documented limits, not ground truth)
  vicinity        changed_in_vicinity_k is true when a later non-merge PR commit,
                  after the reviewed head and before merge/close, deletes or modifies an
                  old-side line within +-k of the anchor (start_line..line), or inserts
                  lines between old lines x and x+1 with min(|anchor-x|, |anchor-x-1|)
                  <= k. The anchor is carried through every later commit's hunks (merge
                  commits shift it but are never credited). A deleted or modified anchor
                  line ends the mapping. A code change near the anchor is a proxy for
                  "addressed", not proof. When the reviewed head is not in the PR commit
                  list (rebase/force push) but the commit still exists, the anchor is
                  mapped through one compare/{reviewed}...{final_head} diff instead
                  (vicinity_method "compare-fallback"; the three-dot diff starts at the
                  merge base, so it may include rebased-in changes). Null when that commit
                  is gone, a later diff is missing, the comment is on the LEFT side, or the
                  finding has no line.
  overlap         post_merge_commit.overlaps_pr_lines compares the commit's old-side hunk
                  ranges with the new-side lines the PR diff added to the same file, with
                  no rebase or intermediate-commit mapping
                  (overlap_method "approximate-no-rebase").
  reply kind      author_reply_kind classifies thread replies by the PR author or the
                  owner with keyword regexes, newest reply first: reject words win over
                  ack words, a question mark or question words give "question", no
                  match gives "none". It is a heuristic.
  next status     next_bot_review_status reads the next non-container bot review's
                  "Previous findings"/"Prior findings" items. An item matches when its
                  severity equals the finding's AND the path basename or >= 2 title tokens
                  (non-stopword, length >= 4) appear in it; the best-scoring item wins and
                  is copied to next_bot_review_line. Informational only: it feeds no
                  addressed definition, because the bot must not judge its own fix.
  superseded_by_head  the first PR commit after the reviewed head in commit order
                  (push boundaries are not visible in the API).
  head at comment / blind_to_bot  issue comments are placed on the last PR commit whose
                  committer date precedes them; a human comment is blind_to_bot when no
                  bot review had been submitted before it. capture_recapture counts it
                  only when its head is at or before the panel target head.
  file_type       path rules only (tests/, *_test.*, build files, docs/*.md); labels may
                  override it.
  limits          the PR commits API returns at most 250 commits and the files API at
                  most 3000 files; per-file patches may be absent for large or binary
                  files. These cases are counted in manifest.json "truncation".
"""
